const faq = [
  { q: 'What does a raven symbolise in different cultures?', a: 'The raven carries different symbolic meanings across cultures, though several themes recur: Wisdom and knowledge (Norse: Odin\'s ravens as instruments of omniscience; Celtic: ravens as oracular birds); Death and the battlefield (Norse, Celtic, Greek: ravens feeding on the slain; Valkyrie associations); Transformation and trickery (Native American: Raven as Trickster-Creator who steals fire/light and reshapes the world); Prophecy and omen (Greek, Roman, Celtic: raven calls as omens); and Creation (Arctic, Pacific Northwest: Raven as creator of the world or bringer of light). The raven\'s intelligence, longevity, black plumage, and association with death through scavenging underlie these diverse but connected symbolic roles.' },
  { q: 'Is a raven a symbol of good or bad luck?', a: 'Whether a raven is a good or bad omen varies by culture and context. In Norse tradition, ravens are associated with Odin, wisdom, and power — positive associations. In Celtic warrior tradition, the raven (Mórrígan\'s bird) is both a battle omen and a sign of victory. In many Western folk traditions, a raven at the window or calling near a home is an ill omen, associated with death. In Pacific Northwest Indigenous traditions, Raven is a beneficent creator-trickster. The same bird holds positive and negative associations simultaneously in many traditions, reflecting its ambiguous character.' },
  { q: 'What does it mean when you see a raven?', a: 'What seeing a raven "means" depends on which cultural framework you apply — there is no single universal meaning. Scientifically, seeing a raven means you are in an area with suitable raven habitat and food resources. In traditional omen interpretation, context matters: a raven observed near a sickbed, cemetery, or during a significant life event was more likely to be interpreted as meaningful than a raven sighted during routine travel. Modern spiritual or New Age interpretations often assign personal meanings derived from various cultural traditions. From a sceptical standpoint, the meaning is what you choose to construct from an encounter with a remarkable, intelligent bird.' },
];
